From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 17:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] tests: give the parallel threading tests headroom on slow
 runners

test_parallel_api_lifecycle and test_parallel_helpers wait for their
four worker threads with a hardcoded result(timeout=45). On the riscv64
runners the lifecycle test takes ~43s when it passes, so the margin is
already gone and an unlucky run trips it with a bare TimeoutError (the
cp313-musllinux leg of 2.12.0 took ~57s and failed; the same wheel
passed on every other leg). Nothing hangs or crashes: the barrier waits
inside the workers still succeed and every other test passes.

Raise the wait to 180s. The assertions inside the workers are unchanged.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [riscv64 CI runners are slower than the fixed 45s margin upstream sized for its own hosts]
---
 tests/test_threads.py | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tests/test_threads.py b/tests/test_threads.py
index 22ae5d9..26b2686 100644
--- a/tests/test_threads.py
+++ b/tests/test_threads.py
@@ -98,7 +98,7 @@ assert not sys._is_gil_enabled(), 'tesserocr enabled the GIL'
             with ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=4) as pool:
                 results = [pool.submit(recognize) for _ in range(4)]
                 for result in results:
-                    result.result(timeout=45)
+                    result.result(timeout=180)
         """)
 
     @unittest.skipUnless(importlib.util.find_spec("PIL"), "Pillow not installed")
@@ -123,5 +123,5 @@ assert not sys._is_gil_enabled(), 'tesserocr enabled the GIL'
             with ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=4) as pool:
                 results = [pool.submit(recognize) for _ in range(4)]
                 for result in results:
-                    result.result(timeout=45)
+                    result.result(timeout=180)
         """)
-- 
2.43.0
